    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent lineup anchored by **Junior Caminero**, who commands the highest efficiency score of the day at 84.24. Benefiting from a prime #3 hole assignment and a massive 16% park factor boost, **Junior Caminero** faces off against an exploitable arm in Baz, making him our cornerstone play. We are also leaning heavily into the speed and situational upside of **Caleb Durbin** (70.40), who draws a favorable matchup against a struggling Wilkinson (8.21 xERA). While **Trea Turner** carries a slightly lower score of 61.05, his elite sprint speed remains critical to our stolen base strategy, and his move to the #2 spot adds significant value despite the challenge posed by Leahy.\n\nThe decision-making process for the lower end of the lineup involved a delicate balance of park factors and platoon splits. **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (67.05) earns a start largely due to a significant 16% park boost against Martinez, helping him overcome a marginal platoon disadvantage. Conversely, **Carson Benge** (44.02) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine. While his power profile is appealing, he failed to crack the starting threshold because he is facing a challenging lefty in Newcomb and currently sits below the efficiency ceiling of our other utility options. We remain cautious with **Yordan Alvarez** (56.07) today; while his raw talent is undeniable, the L/L platoon disadvantage against Basso caps his upside, rendering him a marginal start relative to his usual elite status.\n\nThe Zebras are keeping a close watch on the environment, specifically the wind variables influencing **Chase Meidroth** (42.69). While he barely clears the floor, the 5% wind-out boost was the deciding factor in keeping him in the lineup over bench options like **Pedro Ramirez**, who fell below our 40.0 minimum threshold. With high-intensity matchups against elite arms like Leahy, we are prioritizing players like **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (64.85) and **Kyle Schwarber** (63.01) for their ability to leverage favorable lineup positioning to offset the tactical difficulty of the opposing pitching. All other depth pieces, including **Lars Nootbaar** and **Colt Keith**, remain sidelined due to lineup absences or lack of availability.",
